{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UZYSycMv5tZAoemDxC5YCP","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Queensland Electric Super Highway Yurika charging price per kWh how to pay\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Queensland EV charging no longer free - Servopro\",\"url\":\"https://servopro.com.au/queensland-ev-charging-no-longer-free/\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland extends the Electric Super Highway - electrive.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.electrive.com/2021/06/21/queensland-extends-the-electric-super-highway/\"},{\"title\":\"Yurika EV Charger Esk, QLD\",\"url\":\"https://plugroo.com.au/location/yurika-electric-highway-qld-esk-pryde-st\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland to add 13 charging stations to Electric Vehicle Super Highway - The Driven\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2020/09/10/queensland-to-add-13-charging-stations-to-electric-vehicle-super-highway/\"},{\"title\":\"EV drivers spend average $3 and 34 minutes charging on electric superhighway\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2021/04/09/ev-drivers-spend-average-3-and-34-minutes-charging-on-electric-superhighway/\"},{\"title\":\"Yurika / Electric Highway EV Charger Gunalda, QLD\",\"url\":\"https://plugroo.com.au/location/yurika-electric-highway-qld-gunalda-42-balkin-street\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Stations in Queensland (136 sites)\",\"url\":\"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/queensland/\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland identifies two more sites for $2.5million EV network rollout\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2020/02/17/queensland-identifies-two-more-sites-for-2-5million-ev-network-rollout/\"}]\n\n**Pricing on the Queensland Electric Super Highway (QESH), run by Yurika:**\n\n- **Early pricing was low.** A 20c/kWh fee was introduced in January 2020. RACQ was still quoting about 20c/kWh in 2021.\n- **Current prices are higher and vary by site and charger.** Plugroo, an aggregator listing, shows Esk (50 kW) at $0.30–0.55 and Gunalda (75 kW) at $0.35–0.55. At Gunalda, the listing shows the 22 kW AC plugs at $0.35 and the 75 kW DC plugs at $0.55. Another directory lists Kingaroy at $0.30 per kWh. These are third-party listings, so check the current price at the charger or in the app.\n- **A 45c rate was reported earlier.** An older Servopro article, citing the Brisbane Times, said the fee would be 45 cents per kWh. It also said the Minister was negotiating a lower price. That article appears to be several years old, and the 20c rate it describes was in place in 2020–2021.\n\n**How to pay:**\n- The network is operated through Chargefox. One source says sites are accessed via a smartphone app from Chargefox. The usual method is to create a Chargefox account in the app, add a payment method, and start the session there.\n- The Plugroo listings give Yurika's contact number as 1300 792 611 and its website as yurika.com.au. I didn't find an official payment guide in these results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00999965-fd79-4ff4-93d0-123f38506fe6","uuid":"33579569-7952-4d1e-8383-ae5a3f73455e","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:07:57.957Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Queensland Electric Super Highway Yurika charging price per kWh how to pay","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01PsEzgvmqcRAWceDvekfbVm","content":[{"title":"Queensland EV charging no longer free - Servopro","url":"https://servopro.com.au/queensland-ev-charging-no-longer-free/"},{"title":"Queensland extends the Electric Super Highway - electrive.com","url":"https://www.electrive.com/2021/06/21/queensland-extends-the-electric-super-highway/"},{"title":"Yurika EV Charger Esk, QLD","url":"https://plugroo.com.au/location/yurika-electric-highway-qld-esk-pryde-st"},{"title":"Queensland to add 13 charging stations to Electric Vehicle Super Highway - The Driven","url":"https://thedriven.io/2020/09/10/queensland-to-add-13-charging-stations-to-electric-vehicle-super-highway/"},{"title":"EV drivers spend average $3 and 34 minutes charging on electric superhighway","url":"https://thedriven.io/2021/04/09/ev-drivers-spend-average-3-and-34-minutes-charging-on-electric-superhighway/"},{"title":"Yurika / Electric Highway EV Charger Gunalda, QLD","url":"https://plugroo.com.au/location/yurika-electric-highway-qld-gunalda-42-balkin-street"},{"title":"EV Charging Stations in Queensland (136 sites)","url":"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/queensland/"},{"title":"Queensland identifies two more sites for $2.5million EV network rollout","url":"https://thedriven.io/2020/02/17/queensland-identifies-two-more-sites-for-2-5million-ev-network-rollout/"}]},"**Pricing on the Queensland Electric Super Highway (QESH), run by Yurika:**\n\n- **Early pricing was low.** A 20c/kWh fee was introduced in January 2020. RACQ was still quoting about 20c/kWh in 2021.\n- **Current prices are higher and vary by site and charger.** Plugroo, an aggregator listing, shows Esk (50 kW) at $0.30–0.55 and Gunalda (75 kW) at $0.35–0.55. At Gunalda, the listing shows the 22 kW AC plugs at $0.35 and the 75 kW DC plugs at $0.55. Another directory lists Kingaroy at $0.30 per kWh. These are third-party listings, so check the current price at the charger or in the app.\n- **A 45c rate was reported earlier.** An older Servopro article, citing the Brisbane Times, said the fee would be 45 cents per kWh. It also said the Minister was negotiating a lower price. That article appears to be several years old, and the 20c rate it describes was in place in 2020–2021.\n\n**How to pay:**\n- The network is operated through Chargefox. One source says sites are accessed via a smartphone app from Chargefox. The usual method is to create a Chargefox account in the app, add a payment method, and start the session there.\n- The Plugroo listings give Yurika's contact number as 1300 792 611 and its website as yurika.com.au. I didn't find an official payment guide in these results."],"durationSeconds":5.989456857000001,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UZYSycMv5tZAoemDxC5YCP","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011sWLC7j3UGEfc4MeRUJfVX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"RAA EV charging network South Australia price per kWh app\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"RAA (SA) Roadside Assistance for EV Owners\",\"url\":\"https://evroadside.com.au/providers/raa-ev/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA's South Australian EV Charging Network Completed\",\"url\":\"https://www.solarquotes.com.au/blog/raa-sa-ev-charging-mb3220/\"},{\"title\":\"Australia's Best Public EV Charging Station: And The Winner Is ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.solarquotes.com.au/blog/best-ev-charging-station-mb3044/\"},{\"title\":\"Discover EV charging stations in South Australia — and drive with confidence - Flare\",\"url\":\"https://www.flarehr.com/blog/19710-2\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging & Roadside Assistance in Adelaide\",\"url\":\"https://evroadside.com.au/locations/adelaide/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA to create SA’s first electric vehicle charging network - RAA Daily\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-to-create-sas-first-electric-vehicle-charging-network/\"},{\"title\":\"South Australia’s RAA EV network gets first 150kW rapid charger site\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2023/07/05/south-australias-raa-ev-network-gets-first-150kw-rapid-charger-site/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2026/01/01/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA to roll out 140 new EV charging locations in South Australia in $12.4m plan\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2022/02/14/raa-to-roll-out-140-new-ev-charging-locations-in-south-australia-in-12-4m-plan/\"},{\"title\":\"Cost to Charge an Electric Car in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://evroadside.com.au/guides/cost-to-charge-electric-car/\"}]\n\n**RAA Charge (South Australia): pricing and app**\n\n**App:** Charging sessions and payments are controlled via the Chargefox app, which also shows where the stations are located. RAA members save 10 per cent on charging fees.\n\n**Network:** 140+ sites and 550+ plugs from Yalata to Mount Gambier, completed in 2025; over 75% of sites are regional.\n\n**Most recent pricing (evroadside.com.au, about 159 days old, so roughly mid-2026):**\n- Metro Adelaide AC is 33c/kWh off-peak and 40c/kWh in the evening peak. DC is 66c/kWh off-peak and 75c/kWh peak.\n- Country sites cost 1 to 2 cents more and outback sites 3 to 5 cents more. Across the network, AC runs 33 to 45 cents and DC 66 to 78 cents.\n- The evening peak is 5pm to 10pm and everything outside it is off-peak.\n- A $1 minimum applies to every session. DC rapid sites add a $1-a-minute idle fee once you're 10 minutes past the end of your charge.\n\n**Older pricing (SolarQuotes, about 498 days old):**\n- Destination AC sites were 30c off-peak and 37c peak.\n- Rapid and ultra-rapid sites were 64c standard and 73c in the evening peak.\n- Rates have risen since then.\n\n**Caveat:** Prices change often. One source advises to check the app for the live rate before you plug in.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00999965-fd79-4ff4-93d0-123f38506fe6","uuid":"00a3e6f8-7a1e-4979-9b55-9fd8d9487d6d","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:07:58.048Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"RAA EV charging network South Australia price per kWh app","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01VpXgrBjmGbfnEuB5FZLxvB","content":[{"title":"RAA (SA) Roadside Assistance for EV Owners","url":"https://evroadside.com.au/providers/raa-ev/"},{"title":"RAA's South Australian EV Charging Network Completed","url":"https://www.solarquotes.com.au/blog/raa-sa-ev-charging-mb3220/"},{"title":"Australia's Best Public EV Charging Station: And The Winner Is ...","url":"https://www.solarquotes.com.au/blog/best-ev-charging-station-mb3044/"},{"title":"Discover EV charging stations in South Australia — and drive with confidence - Flare","url":"https://www.flarehr.com/blog/19710-2"},{"title":"EV Charging & Roadside Assistance in Adelaide","url":"https://evroadside.com.au/locations/adelaide/"},{"title":"RAA to create SA’s first electric vehicle charging network - RAA Daily","url":"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-to-create-sas-first-electric-vehicle-charging-network/"},{"title":"South Australia’s RAA EV network gets first 150kW rapid charger site","url":"https://thedriven.io/2023/07/05/south-australias-raa-ev-network-gets-first-150kw-rapid-charger-site/"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2026/01/01/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"RAA to roll out 140 new EV charging locations in South Australia in $12.4m plan","url":"https://thedriven.io/2022/02/14/raa-to-roll-out-140-new-ev-charging-locations-in-south-australia-in-12-4m-plan/"},{"title":"Cost to Charge an Electric Car in Australia","url":"https://evroadside.com.au/guides/cost-to-charge-electric-car/"}]},"**RAA Charge (South Australia): pricing and app**\n\n**App:** Charging sessions and payments are controlled via the Chargefox app, which also shows where the stations are located. RAA members save 10 per cent on charging fees.\n\n**Network:** 140+ sites and 550+ plugs from Yalata to Mount Gambier, completed in 2025; over 75% of sites are regional.\n\n**Most recent pricing (evroadside.com.au, about 159 days old, so roughly mid-2026):**\n- Metro Adelaide AC is 33c/kWh off-peak and 40c/kWh in the evening peak. DC is 66c/kWh off-peak and 75c/kWh peak.\n- Country sites cost 1 to 2 cents more and outback sites 3 to 5 cents more. Across the network, AC runs 33 to 45 cents and DC 66 to 78 cents.\n- The evening peak is 5pm to 10pm and everything outside it is off-peak.\n- A $1 minimum applies to every session. DC rapid sites add a $1-a-minute idle fee once you're 10 minutes past the end of your charge.\n\n**Older pricing (SolarQuotes, about 498 days old):**\n- Destination AC sites were 30c off-peak and 37c peak.\n- Rapid and ultra-rapid sites were 64c standard and 73c in the evening peak.\n- Rates have risen since then.\n\n**Caveat:** Prices change often. One source advises to check the app for the live rate before you plug in."],"durationSeconds":5.507555859,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011sWLC7j3UGEfc4MeRUJfVX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WHbeHhPWqikP5a5tnWqvJ3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Charging the Regions EV charging network Victoria price per kWh operator\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"How much does it cost to charge an EV at home? The 2026–27 numbers, state by state\",\"url\":\"https://evselect.com.au/articles/cost-to-charge-ev-at-home-victoria-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Victoria, British Columbia EV Charging Stations Info\",\"url\":\"https://chargehub.com/en/countries/canada/british-columbia/victoria.html\"},{\"title\":\"Fully charged: Your ultimate handbook to Victoria EV charging stations - Flare\",\"url\":\"https://www.flarehr.com/blog/fully-charged-your-ultimate-handbook-to-ev-charging-stations-in-victoria\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Stations VIC - Find Chargers Near You\",\"url\":\"https://plugroo.com.au/vic\"},{\"title\":\"Electric Vehicle Charging\",\"url\":\"https://www.wellington.vic.gov.au/environment/electric-vehicle-charging\"},{\"title\":\"Electric vehicle charging and energy options in victoria\",\"url\":\"https://vicsolar.com.au/blog/electric-vehicle-charging-and-energy-options-in-victoria/\"},{\"title\":\"NRMA EV Charging Network Introduces Tap n Pay and Location-Based Pricing at Some Locations\",\"url\":\"https://zecar.com/reviews/nrma-ev-charging-network-introduces-tap-n-pay-and-location-based-pricing-at-some-locations\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Stations in Victoria (294 sites)\",\"url\":\"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/victoria/\"},{\"title\":\"New EV Charging Fees Based on Power Used\",\"url\":\"https://www.victoria.ca/city-government/news/new-ev-charging-fees-based-power-used\"}]\n\nThe search turned up no page about the \"Charging the Regions\" network itself. It did give some related pricing.\n\n- **Wellington Shire (Gippsland):** Wellington Shire's planning for charging infrastructure draws on the \"Charging the Regions Local Government EV Charging Network Study\". Its council-owned chargers cost 40c/kWh, paid through either the Evie or Chargefox apps depending on the location. RACV is planned to own and operate a 75kW charger at Stratford. That page is old, so the price may have changed.\n- **Chargefox sites in Victoria:** Moe is listed at 40c/kWh. Airport West and Barnawartha North are at about $0.65/kWh.\n- **Evie sites:** Evie's 350 kW sites, such as Warrenheip, are listed at about $0.60/kWh.\n- **NRMA regional sites:** NRMA's new rates are $0.75/kWh at Ararat, $0.79 at Marong and $0.75 at Wycheproof. That article is about 587 days old.\n- **General Victorian public charging:** Public charging ranges from free destination charging up to $0.85/kWh at ultra-rapid DC chargers.\n\nOperators, mainly Chargefox and Evie, appear to run the council-funded regional chargers, and prices vary by site. I'd search for the study or the specific council sites if you need exact figures.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00999965-fd79-4ff4-93d0-123f38506fe6","uuid":"3cdc3fce-8983-485d-825a-0aeca33220ce","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:07:58.090Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Charging the Regions EV charging network Victoria price per kWh operator","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01HmnD7KsrR4ft5hVffqTmHk","content":[{"title":"How much does it cost to charge an EV at home? The 2026–27 numbers, state by state","url":"https://evselect.com.au/articles/cost-to-charge-ev-at-home-victoria-2026"},{"title":"Victoria, British Columbia EV Charging Stations Info","url":"https://chargehub.com/en/countries/canada/british-columbia/victoria.html"},{"title":"Fully charged: Your ultimate handbook to Victoria EV charging stations - Flare","url":"https://www.flarehr.com/blog/fully-charged-your-ultimate-handbook-to-ev-charging-stations-in-victoria"},{"title":"EV Charging Stations VIC - Find Chargers Near You","url":"https://plugroo.com.au/vic"},{"title":"Electric Vehicle Charging","url":"https://www.wellington.vic.gov.au/environment/electric-vehicle-charging"},{"title":"Electric vehicle charging and energy options in victoria","url":"https://vicsolar.com.au/blog/electric-vehicle-charging-and-energy-options-in-victoria/"},{"title":"NRMA EV Charging Network Introduces Tap n Pay and Location-Based Pricing at Some Locations","url":"https://zecar.com/reviews/nrma-ev-charging-network-introduces-tap-n-pay-and-location-based-pricing-at-some-locations"},{"title":"EV Charging Stations in Victoria (294 sites)","url":"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/victoria/"},{"title":"New EV Charging Fees Based on Power Used","url":"https://www.victoria.ca/city-government/news/new-ev-charging-fees-based-power-used"}]},"The search turned up no page about the \"Charging the Regions\" network itself. It did give some related pricing.\n\n- **Wellington Shire (Gippsland):** Wellington Shire's planning for charging infrastructure draws on the \"Charging the Regions Local Government EV Charging Network Study\". Its council-owned chargers cost 40c/kWh, paid through either the Evie or Chargefox apps depending on the location. RACV is planned to own and operate a 75kW charger at Stratford. That page is old, so the price may have changed.\n- **Chargefox sites in Victoria:** Moe is listed at 40c/kWh. Airport West and Barnawartha North are at about $0.65/kWh.\n- **Evie sites:** Evie's 350 kW sites, such as Warrenheip, are listed at about $0.60/kWh.\n- **NRMA regional sites:** NRMA's new rates are $0.75/kWh at Ararat, $0.79 at Marong and $0.75 at Wycheproof. That article is about 587 days old.\n- **General Victorian public charging:** Public charging ranges from free destination charging up to $0.85/kWh at ultra-rapid DC chargers.\n\nOperators, mainly Chargefox and Evie, appear to run the council-funded regional chargers, and prices vary by site. I'd search for the study or the specific council sites if you need exact figures."],"durationSeconds":5.795967073000001,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WHbeHhPWqikP5a5tnWqvJ3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
