{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019dKjU84j6KDoWkX59n1qWK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"QESH Queensland Electric Super Highway Chargefox app qld.gov.au charging FAQ\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Welcome to the Queensland Electric Super Highway\",\"url\":\"https://www.yurika.com.au/capability/qld-electric-super-highway/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Stations QLD Guide - Auto Stop\",\"url\":\"https://www.autostop.com.au/auto-stop-news/ev-charging-stations-qld-guide/\"},{\"title\":\"Yurika EV Charging Network\",\"url\":\"https://evlog.net.au/yurika-ev-charging-network/\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland identifies two more sites for $2.5million EV network rollout\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2020/02/17/queensland-identifies-two-more-sites-for-2-5million-ev-network-rollout/\"},{\"title\":\"Electric car drivers can now use Chargefox network from Adelaide to Cairns\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2019/07/02/electric-car-drivers-can-now-use-chargefox-network-from-adelaide-to-cairns/\"},{\"title\":\"Third phase of EV Super Highway to add 23 new charging stations\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2024/01/15/third-phase-of-ev-super-highway-to-add-23-new-charging-stations/\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland Electric Highway\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/queensland-electric-highway.76463/page-13\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Stations in Queensland (136 sites)\",\"url\":\"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/queensland/\"},{\"title\":\"Electric dreaming: Discover the 109 EV charging stations in Queensland - Flare\",\"url\":\"https://www.flarehr.com/blog/exploring-ev-charging-stations-in-queensland\"}]\n\n**Summary of results**\n\n- **How to charge:** You need the Chargefox App (iPhone or Android) and must create an account before you plug in. Charges apply. For help, visit chargefox.com or call 1300 518 038.\n- **Plugs:** DC charging uses CHAdeMO and CCS Combo Type 2 cables. AC charging uses a Type 2 Mennekes socket, and you bring your own cable.\n- **Charging time:** The 75kW DC chargers should typically give up to 80% charge in under an hour for most vehicles. Times vary by vehicle.\n- **Cost:** Pricing varies by location, and the Chargefox App shows current prices. Older reports put the rate at 20c/kWh. A more recent listing shows $0.30/kWh at QESH sites such as Kingaroy and Pimpama. Check the app for current pricing.\n- **Network size:** The QESH is a Queensland Government initiative, built and operated by Yurika and supported by RACQ. It has over 50 stations from Coolangatta to Port Douglas, extending into regional Queensland. The completed network is planned at 54 fast-charging locations.\n- **Finding chargers:** You can use PlugShare, or the Chargefox App itself.\n\nThe first result is Yurika's page on the QESH. The search didn't return the qld.gov.au FAQ page itself.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00999965-fd79-4ff4-93d0-123f38506fe6","uuid":"26e65a26-287b-42df-981b-33d4c335d454","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:08:09.591Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"QESH Queensland Electric Super Highway Chargefox app qld.gov.au charging FAQ","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01MWtJLEA6mDQoFixRx33fQz","content":[{"title":"Welcome to the Queensland Electric Super Highway","url":"https://www.yurika.com.au/capability/qld-electric-super-highway/"},{"title":"EV Charging Stations QLD Guide - Auto Stop","url":"https://www.autostop.com.au/auto-stop-news/ev-charging-stations-qld-guide/"},{"title":"Yurika EV Charging Network","url":"https://evlog.net.au/yurika-ev-charging-network/"},{"title":"Queensland identifies two more sites for $2.5million EV network rollout","url":"https://thedriven.io/2020/02/17/queensland-identifies-two-more-sites-for-2-5million-ev-network-rollout/"},{"title":"Electric car drivers can now use Chargefox network from Adelaide to Cairns","url":"https://thedriven.io/2019/07/02/electric-car-drivers-can-now-use-chargefox-network-from-adelaide-to-cairns/"},{"title":"Third phase of EV Super Highway to add 23 new charging stations","url":"https://thedriven.io/2024/01/15/third-phase-of-ev-super-highway-to-add-23-new-charging-stations/"},{"title":"Queensland Electric Highway","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/queensland-electric-highway.76463/page-13"},{"title":"EV Charging Stations in Queensland (136 sites)","url":"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/queensland/"},{"title":"Electric dreaming: Discover the 109 EV charging stations in Queensland - Flare","url":"https://www.flarehr.com/blog/exploring-ev-charging-stations-in-queensland"}]},"**Summary of results**\n\n- **How to charge:** You need the Chargefox App (iPhone or Android) and must create an account before you plug in. Charges apply. For help, visit chargefox.com or call 1300 518 038.\n- **Plugs:** DC charging uses CHAdeMO and CCS Combo Type 2 cables. AC charging uses a Type 2 Mennekes socket, and you bring your own cable.\n- **Charging time:** The 75kW DC chargers should typically give up to 80% charge in under an hour for most vehicles. Times vary by vehicle.\n- **Cost:** Pricing varies by location, and the Chargefox App shows current prices. Older reports put the rate at 20c/kWh. A more recent listing shows $0.30/kWh at QESH sites such as Kingaroy and Pimpama. Check the app for current pricing.\n- **Network size:** The QESH is a Queensland Government initiative, built and operated by Yurika and supported by RACQ. It has over 50 stations from Coolangatta to Port Douglas, extending into regional Queensland. The completed network is planned at 54 fast-charging locations.\n- **Finding chargers:** You can use PlugShare, or the Chargefox App itself.\n\nThe first result is Yurika's page on the QESH. The search didn't return the qld.gov.au FAQ page itself."],"durationSeconds":5.664196302000001,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"