{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PPsPoSe1kALZNdAhipqnfa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"RAA Charge Chargefox app electric vehicle charging South Australia raa.com.au\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EV charging stations\",\"url\":\"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/motoring-services/ev-charging-stations\"},{\"title\":\"Electric vehicles\",\"url\":\"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/ev-hub\"},{\"title\":\"RAA completes South Australia’s first statewide EV charging network - RAA Daily\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-completes-south-australias-first-statewide-ev-charging-network/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA Charging Stations - RAA member discount\",\"url\":\"https://our.raa.com.au/membership/member-discounts-and-offers/ev-charging-stations\"},{\"title\":\"RAA SA Charging Network\",\"url\":\"https://evlog.net.au/raa-sa-charging-network/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA Charge\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-charge-12-electric-vehicle-charging-locations-switched-on-today-as-part-of-network-launch/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA Charge closes the gap in SA-WA crossing for EV drivers - RAA Daily\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-charge-closes-the-gap-in-sa-wa-crossing-for-ev-drivers/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Apps for EVs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2026/10/27/best-ev-charging-apps-for-evs-in-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"techAU interviews RAA: new South Australia EV charger network feat Kempower, Chargefox, JET Charge\",\"url\":\"https://techau.com.au/techau-interviews-raa-new-south-australia-electric-car-charger-network-feat-kempower-chargefox-jet-charge/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA Charge set to expand as SA businesses want in on EV charging services - RAA Daily\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-charge-set-to-expand-as-sa-businesses-want-in-on-ev-charging-services/\"}]\n\nRAA Charge is South Australia's public EV charging network, and you use the Chargefox app to find chargers, start a session and pay.\n\n**Network**\n- It has 140+ locations with over 550 charging plugs, and 75% of the sites are in regional SA.\n- Within the first year of construction, RAA installed more than 100 sites. The network was built with a $12.35 million state government grant.\n- AC destination sites run at 7–22 kW. DC rapid sites run at 60–200 kW.\n\n**How to charge**\n- Download Chargefox for iOS or Android and find a site with the app or RAA's interactive map. Then charge and pay through the app or with an RFID card.\n- AC sites have Type 2 sockets, so you need your own cable. DC sites have cables attached.\n- Rapid and ultra-rapid chargers support CCS2, and some sites also support CHAdeMO.\n\n**Pricing (per RAA's site)**\n- Metro AC costs 40c/kWh in the evening peak and 33c/kWh off-peak. Metro DC costs 75c/kWh in the evening peak and 66c/kWh off-peak.\n- Country and Outback sites cost slightly more.\n- Evening peak applies 5pm–10pm.\n- A $1 minimum charge applies to every session.\n- Idle fees apply at all DC rapid sites. You get a 10-minute grace period after charging finishes, then pay $1 per minute while still plugged in.\n\n**Member discount**\n- RAA members save 10% across the RAA Charge network.\n- To get it, log into Chargefox, select RAA as your member program and add your membership number before the session starts. It can't be applied after a session has begun.\n\nSources: raa.com.au/motor/motoring-services/ev-charging-stations, our.raa.com.au member discount page, and RAA Daily press releases.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00999965-fd79-4ff4-93d0-123f38506fe6","uuid":"2aa3649b-f9e2-46ee-be16-320109bf689c","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:08:10.731Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"RAA Charge Chargefox app electric vehicle charging South Australia raa.com.au","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01PkwoHbnJq1Gwu5vAJKjgLE","content":[{"title":"EV charging stations","url":"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/motoring-services/ev-charging-stations"},{"title":"Electric vehicles","url":"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/ev-hub"},{"title":"RAA completes South Australia’s first statewide EV charging network - RAA Daily","url":"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-completes-south-australias-first-statewide-ev-charging-network/"},{"title":"RAA Charging Stations - RAA member discount","url":"https://our.raa.com.au/membership/member-discounts-and-offers/ev-charging-stations"},{"title":"RAA SA Charging Network","url":"https://evlog.net.au/raa-sa-charging-network/"},{"title":"RAA Charge","url":"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-charge-12-electric-vehicle-charging-locations-switched-on-today-as-part-of-network-launch/"},{"title":"RAA Charge closes the gap in SA-WA crossing for EV drivers - RAA Daily","url":"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-charge-closes-the-gap-in-sa-wa-crossing-for-ev-drivers/"},{"title":"EV Charging Apps for EVs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2026/10/27/best-ev-charging-apps-for-evs-in-australia/"},{"title":"techAU interviews RAA: new South Australia EV charger network feat Kempower, Chargefox, JET Charge","url":"https://techau.com.au/techau-interviews-raa-new-south-australia-electric-car-charger-network-feat-kempower-chargefox-jet-charge/"},{"title":"RAA Charge set to expand as SA businesses want in on EV charging services - RAA Daily","url":"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-charge-set-to-expand-as-sa-businesses-want-in-on-ev-charging-services/"}]},"RAA Charge is South Australia's public EV charging network, and you use the Chargefox app to find chargers, start a session and pay.\n\n**Network**\n- It has 140+ locations with over 550 charging plugs, and 75% of the sites are in regional SA.\n- Within the first year of construction, RAA installed more than 100 sites. The network was built with a $12.35 million state government grant.\n- AC destination sites run at 7–22 kW. DC rapid sites run at 60–200 kW.\n\n**How to charge**\n- Download Chargefox for iOS or Android and find a site with the app or RAA's interactive map. Then charge and pay through the app or with an RFID card.\n- AC sites have Type 2 sockets, so you need your own cable. DC sites have cables attached.\n- Rapid and ultra-rapid chargers support CCS2, and some sites also support CHAdeMO.\n\n**Pricing (per RAA's site)**\n- Metro AC costs 40c/kWh in the evening peak and 33c/kWh off-peak. Metro DC costs 75c/kWh in the evening peak and 66c/kWh off-peak.\n- Country and Outback sites cost slightly more.\n- Evening peak applies 5pm–10pm.\n- A $1 minimum charge applies to every session.\n- Idle fees apply at all DC rapid sites. You get a 10-minute grace period after charging finishes, then pay $1 per minute while still plugged in.\n\n**Member discount**\n- RAA members save 10% across the RAA Charge network.\n- To get it, log into Chargefox, select RAA as your member program and add your membership number before the session starts. It can't be applied after a session has begun.\n\nSources: raa.com.au/motor/motoring-services/ev-charging-stations, our.raa.com.au member discount page, and RAA Daily press releases."],"durationSeconds":7.0908946749999995,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PPsPoSe1kALZNdAhipqnfa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
