{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AC7ZGBMutUMWBYZFcq4NW5","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"WA EV Network Horizon Power Synergy EV charging price per kWh how to pay\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"WA EV Network - Future-Ready Solutions\",\"url\":\"https://www.horizonpower.com.au/your-community/getting-future-ready/electrical-vehicle-fast-charging-network/\"},{\"title\":\"How Much Does it Cost to Charge an Electric Car?\",\"url\":\"https://rac.com.au/horizons/drive/electric-car-charge-cost\"},{\"title\":\"WA EV Network Construction Phase FAQs Overview\",\"url\":\"https://www.northam.wa.gov.au/Profiles/northam/Assets/ClientData/News/EV_NETWORK/WA_EV_Network_Construction_FAQs.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Electricity fees & charges - Horizon Power\",\"url\":\"https://www.horizonpower.com.au/utilities/pricing/\"},{\"title\":\"synergy.net.au CONSTRUCTION NOTICE LETTER\",\"url\":\"https://www.northam.wa.gov.au/Profiles/northam/Assets/ClientData/News/EV_NETWORK/Northam_-_WA_EV_Network_-_Letter_to_Residents_or_Business_Owners.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Electric vehicle charging at home: WA tariffs, costs, and smart strategies\",\"url\":\"https://billwise.com.au/blog/ev-charging-home-wa-tariffs-costs\"},{\"title\":\"Synergy EV Add On Plan 2026: Rates, Times & Who It Suits\",\"url\":\"https://www.talkenergy.com.au/guides/synergy-ev-add-on-plan-perth-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"Home EV Charging: Costs, Savings, and Smart Tips\",\"url\":\"https://www.chargingwa.com.au/blog/home-ev-charging-cost/\"},{\"title\":\"Cheapest Electricity Provider in WA - BLUETTI AU\",\"url\":\"https://www.bluettipower.com.au/blogs/buying-guide/cheapest-electricity-provider-in-wa\"},{\"title\":\"Is a Home EV Charger Worth It in WA? (Cost & ROI Guide) - Electric Vehicle Charging Installations\",\"url\":\"https://evci.com.au/is-a-home-ev-charger-worth-it-in-wa/\"}]\n\n**WA EV Network charging prices (Synergy and Horizon Power)**\n\n- **Rates:** Horizon Power's pricing page lists AC chargers at 0.35 cents/kWh and DC chargers at 0.60 cents/kWh, unchanged for 2026/27. These figures are almost certainly meant as $0.35 and $0.60 per kWh. The earlier construction FAQs state them as $0.60/kWh for DC fast chargers and $0.35/kWh for AC slow chargers.\n- **Idle fee:** DC chargers have an idle fee of $1 per minute once the vehicle is 100% charged. There is no idle fee on AC. A 10-minute grace period applies after full charge.\n- **How to pay:** You can pay via the Chargefox app or credit card. A Synergy construction notice for the Northam site also lists credit card, RFID card and a charge phone app as payment options.\n- **Possible regional difference:** The early FAQs said the $0.35 and $0.60 rates applied to chargers in the South West Interconnected System, and that Horizon Power was still working on pricing for the North West system. Horizon's current page shows a single set of rates, so this may have since been unified.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00999965-fd79-4ff4-93d0-123f38506fe6","uuid":"9e59bacc-006a-4754-8f54-22877f524813","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:08:19.591Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"WA EV Network Horizon Power Synergy EV charging price per kWh how to pay","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01TnsDiipiMsdV9qgbQNoSrz","content":[{"title":"WA EV Network - Future-Ready Solutions","url":"https://www.horizonpower.com.au/your-community/getting-future-ready/electrical-vehicle-fast-charging-network/"},{"title":"How Much Does it Cost to Charge an Electric Car?","url":"https://rac.com.au/horizons/drive/electric-car-charge-cost"},{"title":"WA EV Network Construction Phase FAQs Overview","url":"https://www.northam.wa.gov.au/Profiles/northam/Assets/ClientData/News/EV_NETWORK/WA_EV_Network_Construction_FAQs.pdf"},{"title":"Electricity fees & charges - Horizon Power","url":"https://www.horizonpower.com.au/utilities/pricing/"},{"title":"synergy.net.au CONSTRUCTION NOTICE LETTER","url":"https://www.northam.wa.gov.au/Profiles/northam/Assets/ClientData/News/EV_NETWORK/Northam_-_WA_EV_Network_-_Letter_to_Residents_or_Business_Owners.pdf"},{"title":"Electric vehicle charging at home: WA tariffs, costs, and smart strategies","url":"https://billwise.com.au/blog/ev-charging-home-wa-tariffs-costs"},{"title":"Synergy EV Add On Plan 2026: Rates, Times & Who It Suits","url":"https://www.talkenergy.com.au/guides/synergy-ev-add-on-plan-perth-2026/"},{"title":"Home EV Charging: Costs, Savings, and Smart Tips","url":"https://www.chargingwa.com.au/blog/home-ev-charging-cost/"},{"title":"Cheapest Electricity Provider in WA - BLUETTI AU","url":"https://www.bluettipower.com.au/blogs/buying-guide/cheapest-electricity-provider-in-wa"},{"title":"Is a Home EV Charger Worth It in WA? (Cost & ROI Guide) - Electric Vehicle Charging Installations","url":"https://evci.com.au/is-a-home-ev-charger-worth-it-in-wa/"}]},"**WA EV Network charging prices (Synergy and Horizon Power)**\n\n- **Rates:** Horizon Power's pricing page lists AC chargers at 0.35 cents/kWh and DC chargers at 0.60 cents/kWh, unchanged for 2026/27. These figures are almost certainly meant as $0.35 and $0.60 per kWh. The earlier construction FAQs state them as $0.60/kWh for DC fast chargers and $0.35/kWh for AC slow chargers.\n- **Idle fee:** DC chargers have an idle fee of $1 per minute once the vehicle is 100% charged. There is no idle fee on AC. A 10-minute grace period applies after full charge.\n- **How to pay:** You can pay via the Chargefox app or credit card. A Synergy construction notice for the Northam site also lists credit card, RFID card and a charge phone app as payment options.\n- **Possible regional difference:** The early FAQs said the $0.35 and $0.60 rates applied to chargers in the South West Interconnected System, and that Horizon Power was still working on pricing for the North West system. Horizon's current page shows a single set of rates, so this may have since been unified."],"durationSeconds":5.097093597000002,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AC7ZGBMutUMWBYZFcq4NW5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018r5bRLwiDgYEFzLDrdJ6pw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Electric Highway Tasmania Tasmanian Government charging network operator Chargefox Evie price\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EV Charging Stations in Tasmania (67 sites)\",\"url\":\"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/tasmania/\"},{\"title\":\"Tasmania opens Electric Highway fast-charging network, paving way for EV rentals\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2021/02/19/tasmania-opens-electric-highway-fast-charging-network-paving-way-for-ev-rentals/\"},{\"title\":\"Tasmanian Fast / Ultra Fast chargers\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/tasmanian-fast-ultra-fast-chargers.98249/page-4\"},{\"title\":\"Charging Electric Vehicles Tasmanian Fast Charger Network\",\"url\":\"https://www.aeva.asn.au/files/364/\"},{\"title\":\"84 EV Charging Stations in Tasmania — AU EV Charging Finder\",\"url\":\"https://ev-charging.rollersoft.com.au/state/tas\"},{\"title\":\"DC fast chargers in Tasmania\",\"url\":\"https://www.aeva.asn.au/files/842\"},{\"title\":\"Electric Highway Tasmania - About\",\"url\":\"https://electrichighwaytasmania.com.au/about/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Stations in Tasmania\",\"url\":\"https://evroadside.com.au/chargers/tas/\"},{\"title\":\"Hobart Electric Highway Tasmania Fast Charger Network - Australian Renewable Energy Agency (ARENA)\",\"url\":\"https://arena.gov.au/projects/hobart-electric-highway-tasmania-fast-charger-network-project/\"},{\"title\":\"Tasmanian Fast / Ultra Fast chargers\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/tasmanian-fast-ultra-fast-chargers.98249/page-7\"}]\n\nElectric Highway Tasmania (EHT) is a private company, not a government-run network. The Tasmanian Government has helped fund it through grants.\n\n**Who runs it**\n- EHT is a private company set up in March 2017 by a group of EV enthusiasts. Its aim is a network of fast chargers covering all parts of Tasmania.\n- The first six sites were helped by a $200,000 grant from the Tasmanian Government's ChargeSmart program. A further $320,000 in 2021 funded 10 more sites, installed in 2022/23.\n- EHT uses Chargefox for billing and customer support.\n- One forum post says NRMA owns all of EHT's charging sites. This is a forum claim and I haven't verified it.\n- \"The Tasmanian electric vehicle fast charging network\" is the government's name for all the fast chargers it has supported. EHT operates only some of them (a forum poster's explanation).\n\n**Evie**\n- Evie Networks is a separate operator. It runs ultra-rapid 350 kW sites at Campbell Town, Brighton and Westbury. Evie and Chargefox funded the first two ultra-rapid stations, with ARENA support.\n- Evie's Kingston Town Shopping Centre site is 50 kW.\n\n**Prices**\n- EHT changed its pricing on 8 April 2024. A forum post quoting the notice says it moved to simple per-kWh pricing, replacing the earlier per-kWh plus per-minute fee. The same post says prices range from 50–75c/kWh depending on speed. It also says an idle fee of $0.50 per minute applies on DC chargers, starting 10 minutes after the battery reaches 100%.\n- A directory listing shows Evie at about 60c/kWh at its 350 kW sites and 45c/kWh at Kingston.\n- The same directory lists these Chargefox/EHT-branded sites:\n  - Kings Meadows (350 kW): 65c/kWh.\n  - Kingston: 40–50c/kWh.\n  - Exeter: 70c/kWh.\n- The same directory still shows the old 25c/kWh plus 25c/min structure at some EHT sites, so its data may be out of date.\n- Most Tasmanian sites fall roughly in the 40–70c/kWh range.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00999965-fd79-4ff4-93d0-123f38506fe6","uuid":"95648b7e-8293-4e81-a205-5044e2beca81","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:08:22.252Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Electric Highway Tasmania Tasmanian Government charging network operator Chargefox Evie price","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01AX5E27sFjsRmg1uxZ6VSX4","content":[{"title":"EV Charging Stations in Tasmania (67 sites)","url":"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/tasmania/"},{"title":"Tasmania opens Electric Highway fast-charging network, paving way for EV rentals","url":"https://thedriven.io/2021/02/19/tasmania-opens-electric-highway-fast-charging-network-paving-way-for-ev-rentals/"},{"title":"Tasmanian Fast / Ultra Fast chargers","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/tasmanian-fast-ultra-fast-chargers.98249/page-4"},{"title":"Charging Electric Vehicles Tasmanian Fast Charger Network","url":"https://www.aeva.asn.au/files/364/"},{"title":"84 EV Charging Stations in Tasmania — AU EV Charging Finder","url":"https://ev-charging.rollersoft.com.au/state/tas"},{"title":"DC fast chargers in Tasmania","url":"https://www.aeva.asn.au/files/842"},{"title":"Electric Highway Tasmania - About","url":"https://electrichighwaytasmania.com.au/about/"},{"title":"EV Charging Stations in Tasmania","url":"https://evroadside.com.au/chargers/tas/"},{"title":"Hobart Electric Highway Tasmania Fast Charger Network - Australian Renewable Energy Agency (ARENA)","url":"https://arena.gov.au/projects/hobart-electric-highway-tasmania-fast-charger-network-project/"},{"title":"Tasmanian Fast / Ultra Fast chargers","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/tasmanian-fast-ultra-fast-chargers.98249/page-7"}]},"Electric Highway Tasmania (EHT) is a private company, not a government-run network. The Tasmanian Government has helped fund it through grants.\n\n**Who runs it**\n- EHT is a private company set up in March 2017 by a group of EV enthusiasts. Its aim is a network of fast chargers covering all parts of Tasmania.\n- The first six sites were helped by a $200,000 grant from the Tasmanian Government's ChargeSmart program. A further $320,000 in 2021 funded 10 more sites, installed in 2022/23.\n- EHT uses Chargefox for billing and customer support.\n- One forum post says NRMA owns all of EHT's charging sites. This is a forum claim and I haven't verified it.\n- \"The Tasmanian electric vehicle fast charging network\" is the government's name for all the fast chargers it has supported. EHT operates only some of them (a forum poster's explanation).\n\n**Evie**\n- Evie Networks is a separate operator. It runs ultra-rapid 350 kW sites at Campbell Town, Brighton and Westbury. Evie and Chargefox funded the first two ultra-rapid stations, with ARENA support.\n- Evie's Kingston Town Shopping Centre site is 50 kW.\n\n**Prices**\n- EHT changed its pricing on 8 April 2024. A forum post quoting the notice says it moved to simple per-kWh pricing, replacing the earlier per-kWh plus per-minute fee. The same post says prices range from 50–75c/kWh depending on speed. It also says an idle fee of $0.50 per minute applies on DC chargers, starting 10 minutes after the battery reaches 100%.\n- A directory listing shows Evie at about 60c/kWh at its 350 kW sites and 45c/kWh at Kingston.\n- The same directory lists these Chargefox/EHT-branded sites:\n  - Kings Meadows (350 kW): 65c/kWh.\n  - Kingston: 40–50c/kWh.\n  - Exeter: 70c/kWh.\n- The same directory still shows the old 25c/kWh plus 25c/min structure at some EHT sites, so its data may be out of date.\n- Most Tasmanian sites fall roughly in the 40–70c/kWh range."],"durationSeconds":8.084405937,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018r5bRLwiDgYEFzLDrdJ6pw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
