{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EgE3DYq57KJU7rxVz8ceY9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"WeVolt EV charging Western Australia network price per kWh\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Transperth Electric Vehicle Charger Trial\",\"url\":\"https://www.mysaytransport.wa.gov.au/pta-ev-chargers\"},{\"title\":\"Electric Vehicle Chargers\",\"url\":\"https://www.transperth.wa.gov.au/Using-Transperth/Station-Facilities/Electric-Vehicle-Chargers\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2026/01/01/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Is a Home EV Charger Worth It in WA? (Cost & ROI Guide) - Electric Vehicle Charging Installations\",\"url\":\"https://evci.com.au/is-a-home-ev-charger-worth-it-in-wa/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2025/09/20/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"How Much Does It Cost to Charge an EV in Australia? (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://evcharginglocations.com.au/blog/ev-charging-cost-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2025/12/23/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"WA EV Network - Future-Ready Solutions\",\"url\":\"https://www.horizonpower.com.au/your-community/getting-future-ready/electrical-vehicle-fast-charging-network/\"},{\"title\":\"How Much Does It Cost to Charge an Electric Car in Australia? (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://www.helloelectrical.com.au/blog/how-much-does-it-cost-to-charge-an-ev-at-home-in-australia\"},{\"title\":\"What Is the Real Cost Per kWh at Australian Public Charging Stations?\",\"url\":\"https://fuelsavingtips.com.au/ev-charging-cost-australia-public-stations/\"}]\n\n**Summary of WeVolt pricing in Western Australia:**\n\n- **Transperth station chargers (the one confirmed WA rate):** Wevolt operates these on behalf of the Public Transport Authority. Effective 7 January 2026, the charging fee at all stations is a usage charge of $0.43 per kWh. This pricing applies for a limited time only while the trial is monitored. These chargers deliver up to 7kW, taking about eight hours to charge a typical EV. Users also need to pay the $2 SmartParker fee. Users must bring their own Type-2 cable.\n\n- **Wevolt's wider DC network (national, not WA-specific):** Third-party trackers give differing ranges. One lists 45–75c/kWh. A later update shows 35–73c/kWh. An older one shows 0–65c/kWh.\n\n- **Other WA networks, for comparison:** Horizon Power's WA EV Network (a separate network) lists AC and DC electricity charges, plus a $1 per minute idle fee on DC once the car reaches 100%. That page is old, and its units look garbled (it says \"0.35c\" and \"0.60c\", which probably means 35c and 60c per kWh).\n\nPrices vary by site and change over time, so check the Wevolt app or the Transperth page for current rates.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00999965-fd79-4ff4-93d0-123f38506fe6","uuid":"cf208391-a475-4330-b196-7228368494f8","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:08:40.687Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"WeVolt EV charging Western Australia network price per kWh","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014LHGdw7nR8diXeyxrZAECz","content":[{"title":"Transperth Electric Vehicle Charger Trial","url":"https://www.mysaytransport.wa.gov.au/pta-ev-chargers"},{"title":"Electric Vehicle Chargers","url":"https://www.transperth.wa.gov.au/Using-Transperth/Station-Facilities/Electric-Vehicle-Chargers"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2026/01/01/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"Is a Home EV Charger Worth It in WA? (Cost & ROI Guide) - Electric Vehicle Charging Installations","url":"https://evci.com.au/is-a-home-ev-charger-worth-it-in-wa/"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2025/09/20/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"How Much Does It Cost to Charge an EV in Australia? (2026)","url":"https://evcharginglocations.com.au/blog/ev-charging-cost-australia/"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2025/12/23/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"WA EV Network - Future-Ready Solutions","url":"https://www.horizonpower.com.au/your-community/getting-future-ready/electrical-vehicle-fast-charging-network/"},{"title":"How Much Does It Cost to Charge an Electric Car in Australia? (2026)","url":"https://www.helloelectrical.com.au/blog/how-much-does-it-cost-to-charge-an-ev-at-home-in-australia"},{"title":"What Is the Real Cost Per kWh at Australian Public Charging Stations?","url":"https://fuelsavingtips.com.au/ev-charging-cost-australia-public-stations/"}]},"**Summary of WeVolt pricing in Western Australia:**\n\n- **Transperth station chargers (the one confirmed WA rate):** Wevolt operates these on behalf of the Public Transport Authority. Effective 7 January 2026, the charging fee at all stations is a usage charge of $0.43 per kWh. This pricing applies for a limited time only while the trial is monitored. These chargers deliver up to 7kW, taking about eight hours to charge a typical EV. Users also need to pay the $2 SmartParker fee. Users must bring their own Type-2 cable.\n\n- **Wevolt's wider DC network (national, not WA-specific):** Third-party trackers give differing ranges. One lists 45–75c/kWh. A later update shows 35–73c/kWh. An older one shows 0–65c/kWh.\n\n- **Other WA networks, for comparison:** Horizon Power's WA EV Network (a separate network) lists AC and DC electricity charges, plus a $1 per minute idle fee on DC once the car reaches 100%. That page is old, and its units look garbled (it says \"0.35c\" and \"0.60c\", which probably means 35c and 60c per kWh).\n\nPrices vary by site and change over time, so check the Wevolt app or the Transperth page for current rates."],"durationSeconds":5.491565861000002,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EgE3DYq57KJU7rxVz8ceY9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015VLcqfuFhqxybyzEEktvZw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Electrona Tasmania EV charging network price per kWh Coles Bay Bicheno\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"DC fast chargers in Tasmania\",\"url\":\"https://www.aeva.asn.au/files/842\"},{\"title\":\"Bicheno Town Centre\",\"url\":\"https://www.plugshare.com/location/494062\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Stations in Tasmania (67 sites)\",\"url\":\"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/tasmania/\"},{\"title\":\"Tasmanian Fast / Ultra Fast chargers\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/tasmanian-fast-ultra-fast-chargers.98249/page-4\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Stations in Bicheno\",\"url\":\"https://evcharginglocations.com.au/tasmania/bicheno/\"},{\"title\":\"Tasmanian Fast / Ultra Fast chargers\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/tasmanian-fast-ultra-fast-chargers.98249/page-7\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charger Installers Bicheno TAS: $1,400-$3,000 (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://pumpswap.com.au/ev-charger/installers/tas/bicheno\"},{\"title\":\"Charging Electric Vehicles Tasmanian Fast Charger Network\",\"url\":\"https://www.aeva.asn.au/files/364/\"},{\"title\":\"Electrona Pty Ltd — Energy projects\",\"url\":\"https://www.electrona.com.au/projects.html\"},{\"title\":\"Tasmania Powers Up: 11 New Public EV Charging Stations Coming Statewide\",\"url\":\"https://zecar.com/reviews/tasmania-11-new-public-ev-charging-stations\"}]\n\n**Electrona pricing (Bicheno):**\n- Electrona's Bicheno Town Centre charger is at 39 Foster St. PlugShare lists CCS/CHAdeMO DC at $0.65 per kWh and the Type 2 AC socket at $0.50 per kWh.\n- DC charging is limited to 2 hours. After that an idle fee of $0.50/min applies. AC time is uncapped.\n- Payment is by the on-board credit card reader with no app needed. A $50 refundable pre-authorization applies. A third-party site says the pre-authorisation is $60, so the figure may have changed.\n- Another aggregator puts Bicheno charging at roughly $0.60 per kWh.\n- PlugShare notes that this location has variable pricing. The official Electrona price page is electrona.au/evc/bchno/bchno-001.html.\n\n**Coles Bay:**\n- Electrona's projects page says new fast chargers are coming to Bothwell, Coles Bay, Orford and Port Arthur, funded by the ChargeSmart Grants Program.\n- I found no published Coles Bay pricing. It may not be open yet, and the results don't say.\n\n**Context:** An AEVA fact sheet says Tasmanian DC fast-charger prices vary by operator and speed. Most are roughly 40c to 70c per kWh.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00999965-fd79-4ff4-93d0-123f38506fe6","uuid":"0fcf65a7-3e1b-47cf-a6fb-55b0263e2caf","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:08:40.974Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Electrona Tasmania EV charging network price per kWh Coles Bay Bicheno","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Ui52Fgt2PeJdB5sejoe7fj","content":[{"title":"DC fast chargers in Tasmania","url":"https://www.aeva.asn.au/files/842"},{"title":"Bicheno Town Centre","url":"https://www.plugshare.com/location/494062"},{"title":"EV Charging Stations in Tasmania (67 sites)","url":"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/tasmania/"},{"title":"Tasmanian Fast / Ultra Fast chargers","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/tasmanian-fast-ultra-fast-chargers.98249/page-4"},{"title":"EV Charging Stations in Bicheno","url":"https://evcharginglocations.com.au/tasmania/bicheno/"},{"title":"Tasmanian Fast / Ultra Fast chargers","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/tasmanian-fast-ultra-fast-chargers.98249/page-7"},{"title":"EV Charger Installers Bicheno TAS: $1,400-$3,000 (2026)","url":"https://pumpswap.com.au/ev-charger/installers/tas/bicheno"},{"title":"Charging Electric Vehicles Tasmanian Fast Charger Network","url":"https://www.aeva.asn.au/files/364/"},{"title":"Electrona Pty Ltd — Energy projects","url":"https://www.electrona.com.au/projects.html"},{"title":"Tasmania Powers Up: 11 New Public EV Charging Stations Coming Statewide","url":"https://zecar.com/reviews/tasmania-11-new-public-ev-charging-stations"}]},"**Electrona pricing (Bicheno):**\n- Electrona's Bicheno Town Centre charger is at 39 Foster St. PlugShare lists CCS/CHAdeMO DC at $0.65 per kWh and the Type 2 AC socket at $0.50 per kWh.\n- DC charging is limited to 2 hours. After that an idle fee of $0.50/min applies. AC time is uncapped.\n- Payment is by the on-board credit card reader with no app needed. A $50 refundable pre-authorization applies. A third-party site says the pre-authorisation is $60, so the figure may have changed.\n- Another aggregator puts Bicheno charging at roughly $0.60 per kWh.\n- PlugShare notes that this location has variable pricing. The official Electrona price page is electrona.au/evc/bchno/bchno-001.html.\n\n**Coles Bay:**\n- Electrona's projects page says new fast chargers are coming to Bothwell, Coles Bay, Orford and Port Arthur, funded by the ChargeSmart Grants Program.\n- I found no published Coles Bay pricing. It may not be open yet, and the results don't say.\n\n**Context:** An AEVA fact sheet says Tasmanian DC fast-charger prices vary by operator and speed. Most are roughly 40c to 70c per kWh."],"durationSeconds":6.0278330219999985,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015VLcqfuFhqxybyzEEktvZw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016xBfjohrXHjkTF97s7xKYr","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Exploren EV charging network Australia Victoria Engie chargers price per kWh\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EV Charging Networks Australia 2026 Compared\",\"url\":\"https://www.gridly.com.au/blog/ev-charging-networks-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Best EV Charging Networks in Australia (2025)\",\"url\":\"https://zecar.com/resources/what-ev-charging-providers-are-in-australia\"},{\"title\":\"Exploren EV charging prices in Australia: rates and fees\",\"url\":\"https://costtocharge.com.au/public-charging-prices/exploren/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2025/12/23/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Everything You Need to Know About Australia’s Public EV Charging Networks (2024) - EV Charge Card\",\"url\":\"https://www.evchargecard.com.au/p/everything-you-need-to-know-about-australias-public-ev-charging-networks/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2025/09/20/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Cost\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2026/05/03/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"How Much Does It Cost to Charge an Electric Car in Australia? (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://www.helloelectrical.com.au/blog/how-much-does-it-cost-to-charge-an-ev-at-home-in-australia\"},{\"title\":\"How Much Does It Cost to Charge an EV in Australia? (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://evcharginglocations.com.au/blog/ev-charging-cost-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Exploren EV charging network (Including Engie)\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/engie-australian-ev-charging-network.239616/page-3\"}]\n\nExploren doesn't have one national price. Site owners set the rates, so they vary by location.\n\n**Engie and Exploren**\n- Exploren acquired Engie's DC network in 2025, adding 230-plus DC fast-charging ports at 80-plus sites.\n\n**Typical prices per kWh**\n- **DC at former Engie and other Exploren sites:** A Gridly comparison says DC sites charge around 45 c/kWh. A user also reports a local Exploren 60kW DC charger at 45c/kWh.\n- **Wider DC range:** Zecar lists $0.55-$0.75/kWh for DC fast chargers. One tracker puts the full Exploren range at 30 to 104 c/kWh.\n- **AC:** Gridly gives a range of Free–55 c/kWh, and many AC sites are free because councils or shopping centres fund them.\n\n**Victoria examples**\n- A forum post says Victoria Gardens, Richmond is charging $0.45/kWh, listed as up to 100kW. That post is old, so the price may have changed.\n- Cost to Charge lists a Kingston Village Square, Ocean Grove, VIC site at 55c/kWh, from a source dated 2026-10-24.\n\n**Other costs**\n- Drivers report card pre-authorisation holds of about $10 on some Exploren sites. These figures come from owners and aren't published by Exploren.\n- Check the Exploren app before charging, because prices vary by site.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00999965-fd79-4ff4-93d0-123f38506fe6","uuid":"83b87b59-90e4-4bb0-9524-d4652ab18aa2","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:08:41.018Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Exploren EV charging network Australia Victoria Engie chargers price per kWh","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01SKQWRPCPZH8bNXjVZQTX2G","content":[{"title":"EV Charging Networks Australia 2026 Compared","url":"https://www.gridly.com.au/blog/ev-charging-networks-australia/"},{"title":"Best EV Charging Networks in Australia (2025)","url":"https://zecar.com/resources/what-ev-charging-providers-are-in-australia"},{"title":"Exploren EV charging prices in Australia: rates and fees","url":"https://costtocharge.com.au/public-charging-prices/exploren/"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2025/12/23/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"Everything You Need to Know About Australia’s Public EV Charging Networks (2024) - EV Charge Card","url":"https://www.evchargecard.com.au/p/everything-you-need-to-know-about-australias-public-ev-charging-networks/"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2025/09/20/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"EV Charging Cost","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2026/05/03/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"How Much Does It Cost to Charge an Electric Car in Australia? (2026)","url":"https://www.helloelectrical.com.au/blog/how-much-does-it-cost-to-charge-an-ev-at-home-in-australia"},{"title":"How Much Does It Cost to Charge an EV in Australia? (2026)","url":"https://evcharginglocations.com.au/blog/ev-charging-cost-australia/"},{"title":"Exploren EV charging network (Including Engie)","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/engie-australian-ev-charging-network.239616/page-3"}]},"Exploren doesn't have one national price. Site owners set the rates, so they vary by location.\n\n**Engie and Exploren**\n- Exploren acquired Engie's DC network in 2025, adding 230-plus DC fast-charging ports at 80-plus sites.\n\n**Typical prices per kWh**\n- **DC at former Engie and other Exploren sites:** A Gridly comparison says DC sites charge around 45 c/kWh. A user also reports a local Exploren 60kW DC charger at 45c/kWh.\n- **Wider DC range:** Zecar lists $0.55-$0.75/kWh for DC fast chargers. One tracker puts the full Exploren range at 30 to 104 c/kWh.\n- **AC:** Gridly gives a range of Free–55 c/kWh, and many AC sites are free because councils or shopping centres fund them.\n\n**Victoria examples**\n- A forum post says Victoria Gardens, Richmond is charging $0.45/kWh, listed as up to 100kW. That post is old, so the price may have changed.\n- Cost to Charge lists a Kingston Village Square, Ocean Grove, VIC site at 55c/kWh, from a source dated 2026-10-24.\n\n**Other costs**\n- Drivers report card pre-authorisation holds of about $10 on some Exploren sites. These figures come from owners and aren't published by Exploren.\n- Check the Exploren app before charging, because prices vary by site."],"durationSeconds":6.463873309999995,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016xBfjohrXHjkTF97s7xKYr","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
