{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChAHji7uBEA2iyUbsFHmq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've opened a pull request for `networks.json`. It adds four networks and folds four operators into existing ones. `validate.mjs` passed. I didn't change any existing typical price, because I found no evidence that any has moved.\n\n**Added**\n- **WA EV Network:** typical $0.60 per kWh, covering Horizon Power's sites. The figure comes from Horizon Power's pricing page as search returned it, because the page itself refused my fetch.\n- **Exploren:** `siteReading` is `forbidden` and the price is null. I also matched \"engie\" to it, since search results agree Exploren took over Engie's DC network in 2025.\n- **Electrona and WeVolt:** both have null prices, since I found no source that states a typical price.\n\n**Folded into Chargefox**\n- **Yurika and Queensland Electric Super Highway:** Yurika's page and a search summary say you charge through the Chargefox app.\n- **RAA:** RAA's own page says you charge and pay in the Chargefox app.\n- **Electric Highway Tasmania:** search results say it uses Chargefox for billing. That one rests on search results, not a page I opened.\n\n**Left undecided**\n- **Charging the Regions:** it looks like a council programme whose sites run through Chargefox or Evie, depending on the site. It stays pending in memory.\n- **Woolworths:** recorded as a site owner only.\n\nThe short match text \"raa\" could hit an unrelated site name, so I flagged it in the pull request.\n\nNo network's price is more than six months old, so I raised no issue. Memory is saved to `operators.json` with a decision for all 12 operators."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1188,"cache_read_input_tokens":55515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1188,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens